1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:54,596
"<i>However, the patient died</i>
<i>two months after surgery."</i>

3
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,475
<i>"The patient's cause of death</i>
<i>remains unknown."</i>

4
00:00:59,601 --> 00:01:01,061
<i>"Upon being asked by a reporter</i>

5
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:03,605
<i>whether they would file</i>
<i>a medical malpractice suit,</i>

6
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:06,066
<i>the bereaved family declined to comment."</i>

7
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:28,129
<i>"The name of the surgeon</i>
<i>was never revealed."</i>

8
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:30,799
<i>"But the alias written on the chart was</i>

9
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:32,383
<i>Doctor X."</i>

10
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:33,760
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

11
00:01:34,928 --> 00:01:36,888
Dr. Gye Su-jeong, are you all right?

12
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:41,601
Are you all right, Doctor?

13
00:01:47,398 --> 00:01:51,569
EPISODE 3

14
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:53,238
<i>So then…</i>

15
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:56,741
<i>What you're saying is</i>
<i>Dr. Gye Su-jeong is Doctor X?</i>

16
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:00,286
Take a good look at the caption here.

17
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:03,123
- Hmm?
- "The surgical team."

18
00:02:03,206 --> 00:02:05,875
There's one Asian person
in a white coat here.

19
00:02:07,001 --> 00:02:09,712
Uh, man. Why is it so blurry?
Damn it!

20
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,089
Dr. Bae.

21
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:14,008
This is basically just a rumor.

22
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:15,093
You believe this?

23
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:17,804
Uh, so what we're saying is that

24
00:02:17,887 --> 00:02:19,848
there's an issue
with that surgical technique.

25
00:02:19,931 --> 00:02:22,851
If Dr. Gye followed this
surgical technique as a reference,

26
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:26,771
then our patient could end up like this
in a couple of months…

27
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,691
Then that's all the more reason
not to let her go.

28
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:34,070
If something goes wrong,
we need someone to take responsibility.

29
00:02:34,988 --> 00:02:36,156
The primary surgeon here was…

30
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:39,409
Dr. Do Yun-sik, after all.

31
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:49,836
The contract doesn't
specify any department.

32
00:02:49,919 --> 00:02:51,588
Oh, well maybe, um…

33
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:56,176
Let's get Dr. Gye Su-jeong in here.

34
00:02:56,759 --> 00:03:01,139
Well, uh, the thing is…
she actually hasn't come in just yet.

35
00:03:01,764 --> 00:03:02,891
My goodness.

36
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:04,601
Good morning, Ms. Jang, we're here.

37
00:03:06,686 --> 00:03:08,146
You're greeting her in Spanish?

38
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:09,689
Come on!

39
00:03:09,772 --> 00:03:12,650
Oh, look at you go, huh? Any more?

40
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:15,987
I'm memorizing morning greetings from
around the world to help prevent dementia.

41
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:17,780
- I guess that makes sense.
- Move! Move!

42
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:19,574
- I need to go out.
- Huh? Why?

43
00:03:21,326 --> 00:03:23,661
Apparently, our girl Su-jeong
chose to play hookayy today.

44
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:25,288
- And she's not picking up either.
- Huh?

45
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:27,332
Must be resting then.
She's always at work or here.

46
00:03:27,415 --> 00:03:29,959
Ms. Jang would know.
We should go and help look.

47
00:03:30,043 --> 00:03:31,336
Hold on a minute.

48
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:32,545
Where have you been all day?

49
00:03:33,129 --> 00:03:35,590
What have you been doing?
I heard you're not at work yet?

50
00:03:35,673 --> 00:03:37,634
Jo Won-jin? Who's Jo Won-jin?

51
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:39,886
Why are you?
Why do you have Su-jeong's… Oh, my God!

52
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:42,513
Dr. Jo Won-jin!

53
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:45,725
Oh, yeah. Yes, I know who you are.
You're the anesthes…

54
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:48,728
You're saying Dr. Gye is in the hospital?

55
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:53,066
So then she did go in to work.

56
00:03:56,694 --> 00:03:58,613
Thank goodness it wasn't worse.

57
00:03:58,696 --> 00:04:00,907
Yeah, we were also able to give her
a transfusion right away.

58
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:01,991
Dr. Gye!

59
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:04,827
Dr. Gye are you--

60
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:06,287
I'm sorry for intruding.

61
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:09,499
Did he not understand
what I said to him before or what?

62
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:11,209
What? Is that kid a doctor?

63
00:04:11,292 --> 00:04:13,753
He's an intern, but honestly,
he seems more like the village idiot.

64
00:04:14,796 --> 00:04:15,964
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

65
00:04:16,047 --> 00:04:18,258
Huh? Oh! Dr. Jo.

66
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:20,927
Please! Save Dr. Gye.
Please, Dr. Jo! Please!

67
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:22,637
Please save her. Please save her, Doctor.

68
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,180
Dr. Park, don't shake--

69
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:27,016
I don't think you understood
what I told you over the phone earlier.

70
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:28,434
I get it completely.
I heard what you said.

71
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:30,645
I can give her a transfusion.
I've got healthy blood and I'm consenting.

72
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:32,230
You certainly misunderstood.

73
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:34,232
The future of Korean medicine
is right here.

74
00:04:35,483 --> 00:04:37,277
Yeah, the doctor's in that bed.
She's just laying over there.

75
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,444
- For real?
- Yeah. Um…

76
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:39,946
Hey, hey.

77
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:43,700
Dr. Gye.

78
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:46,327
Doctor, are you okay?
It's me, Tae-gyeong.

79
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:48,246
Oh! What do we do? Oh, God!

80
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:49,914
We need a blood transfusion, Dr. Kim.

81
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:52,542
You have to save her.
Dr. Kim, please, you have to. Please!

82
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:54,252
- You have to save Dr. Gye. You have to!
- Hey! Hey!

83
00:04:54,335 --> 00:04:56,546
Hey! Hey! If anyone needs to be saved
it's me, you punk!

84
00:04:56,629 --> 00:04:57,964
- Oh, no.
- Where's he working?

85
00:04:58,047 --> 00:05:00,383
Not anesthesiology. So we get that solace.

86
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:02,885
You can't go now, don't go!

87
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:04,512
Get it together, you're acting insane.

88
00:05:04,595 --> 00:05:06,848
Can you stop him, or he'll do CPR.

89
00:05:06,931 --> 00:05:08,516
What are you doing, Doctor? Huh?

90
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:10,893
And how did you even
get this intern gig, honestly?

91
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:11,978
Hello, Director.

92
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:16,399
Ugh, here we go again.

93
00:05:20,236 --> 00:05:21,237
1 HOUR AGO

94
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:22,322
Clear the way!

95
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:26,409
Is the blood ready yet?

96
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:28,828
Uh, not yet. We've been
short on blood recently.

97
00:05:28,911 --> 00:05:30,496
- Blood type?
- AB.

98
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,665
Any match here? Oh, shit. okay.

99
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:35,335
- Go find somebody with AB blood! Hurry up.
- I'm type AB.

100
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:36,419
I'll take her, Doctor.

101
00:05:37,378 --> 00:05:39,505
She has a couple of abrasions

102
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:41,049
and she cried herself to sleep
'cause she was scared.

103
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:43,343
- okay, got it.
- Doctor, you're bleeding right now too.

104
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:46,137
Oh, this blood isn't mine.
all right, let's do it.

105
00:05:47,472 --> 00:05:49,599
- Hurry, prepare for a transfusion.
- Yes, Doctor. On it.

106
00:05:49,682 --> 00:05:51,768
Dr. Gye, wait. Have you eaten today?

107
00:05:51,851 --> 00:05:52,894
Plenty.

108
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:55,521
What are you waiting on?

109
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:58,358
Right now, we're losing blood faster
than we're losing time here.

110
00:05:59,859 --> 00:06:03,780
Uh, there's just no way that
she said something that cool.

111
00:06:03,863 --> 00:06:05,990
Just by her face,
it really doesn't look like it.

112
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:08,576
Hold on. Is she really snoring right now?

113
00:06:08,659 --> 00:06:10,328
Or is it just me who's hearing that?

114
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:11,537
Sometimes, I think…

115
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:14,123
Hmm…

116
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:15,625
When Dr. Gye talks normally,

117
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:18,503
I find it gives me this
sort of a strange vibe.

118
00:06:18,586 --> 00:06:19,629
I know what you're saying, Doctor.

119
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:22,256
You picked up on it as well?
That's the same thing I noticed too.

120
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,300
What are you saying?
Just stay quiet.

121
00:06:24,384 --> 00:06:27,178
Cut it out, all of you. Why are you
acting this way with a patient in the bed?

122
00:06:27,261 --> 00:06:28,638
But "patient," you said?

123
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:32,308
She's down for a nap in the ER and
you're gonna refer to her as a patient?

124
00:06:32,392 --> 00:06:35,269
Anyone lying in an ER bed is a patient,
and my responsibility.

125
00:06:35,353 --> 00:06:37,021
And we also have other patients here, too.

126
00:06:37,563 --> 00:06:39,023
She was on the scene of an accident,

127
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:41,192
assisted with the rescue,
and donated blood as well.

128
00:06:41,275 --> 00:06:43,403
Yeah, so Dr. Gye is pretty amazing,
right, Dr, Jo?

129
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:45,822
It looks like her amazingness
is clearly exhausting.

130
00:06:45,905 --> 00:06:47,198
What the heck. This is embarrassing.

131
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:49,242
I don't get why no one
is praising Dr. Gye.

132
00:06:49,325 --> 00:06:51,994
She went above and beyond
to do her duty as a doctor.

133
00:06:52,078 --> 00:06:54,539
You should all ponder that
as I head over to the operating room.

134
00:06:57,417 --> 00:07:00,586
Duty equals money to her.
That's her only concern.

135
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:03,089
- I wonder what she'll charge us for this.
- Hmm.

136
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:17,103
Has the accident been resolved, Doctor?

137
00:07:17,186 --> 00:07:19,689
Yes. And there were no fatalities either,
thank God.

138
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:21,858
With the person who got
the blood transfusion aside,

139
00:07:22,358 --> 00:07:25,027
no one was seriously hurt,
even though the accident was pretty bad.

140
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:26,195
Well, good job handling it.

141
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:29,073
Director, we'd better go soon.
It's almost time for the conference.

142
00:07:29,157 --> 00:07:30,741
Wait, you're already going?

143
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:31,784
Really, just like that?

144
00:07:33,035 --> 00:07:36,330
Ah, so you came all this way
just to check on a member of your staff.

145
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:38,624
What are you saying?

146
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:42,128
It's just, it seems like a century
since you all last came by.

147
00:07:42,211 --> 00:07:44,338
Now you're here with
the new hospital director at your side

148
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:46,382
to come and grace us with his presence.

149
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:49,385
I suppose I was hoping for something more,
but no, you're just gonna leave?

150
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:51,262
I'm sensing some sarcasm there,
Dr. Seong-jin.

151
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:53,222
I'm just a bit on edge
'cause I haven't slept in two days.

152
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:55,183
And yes, that was sarcasm.

153
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:58,728
You're far from the only one struggling.
I hardly got home last night as well.

154
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:00,938
Naturally, almost all cases
should get handled in Emergency.

155
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:03,232
Or is that not what
Emergency actually does here?

156
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:04,317
Ah!

157
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:08,029
I see, so the ER is here to treat
the patients that aren't worth your time.

158
00:08:08,112 --> 00:08:09,530
That's how you see Emergency?

159
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:11,574
So that's why no one was around back then?

160
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:13,117
What are you talking about?

161
00:08:13,201 --> 00:08:14,660
That's exactly what you're saying, Doctor.

162
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:16,329
That we couldn't handle
that case back then,

163
00:08:16,412 --> 00:08:18,581
- and that's why Seo Jin-yeo--
- Quiet.

164
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:27,632
- Let's take care of the ER's request now.
- Yes, Director.

165
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:33,596
This is a hospital,
we never have enough doctors.

166
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:36,766
But for your sake,
to give you a hand in the ER,

167
00:08:36,849 --> 00:08:38,935
I'll send another doctor temporarily.

168
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:41,896
What? Just like that?

169
00:08:41,979 --> 00:08:43,689
When are they starting?

170
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:46,526
She's right here as we speak.

171
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:47,610
What?

172
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,240
So that snoring lady…

173
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,993
Good luck, Doctor.

174
00:09:00,164 --> 00:09:02,166
No. Go away.

175
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:08,589
What specialty are you?

176
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:10,341
None. I'm an intern.

177
00:09:10,424 --> 00:09:13,553
But I was just been assigned
to accompany Dr. Gye for now.

178
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,388
Really?

179
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:20,142
<i>At around 8:20 a.m. this morning</i>
<i>a school bus and a one-ton truck…</i>

180
00:09:20,226 --> 00:09:21,310
look, the news is on.

181
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:24,730
<i>…collided at Dodam Intersection</i>
<i>in Seongnam, Gyeonggi-do.</i>

182
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:26,440
<i>Five people were seriously injured,</i>

183
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:28,985
<i>but there were no fatalities.</i>

184
00:09:29,068 --> 00:09:31,571
Hey, so, Su-jeong isn't going to get
scolded again today, is she?

185
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:33,239
No, I doubt she'll get scolded.

186
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:35,825
- She only did what a doctor should.
<i>- Now, our next story,</i>

187
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:38,578
<i>on Guseo University Medical Center,</i>
<i>and EMT Seo Jin-yeong,</i>

188
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:42,623
<i>who tragically died a year ago</i>
<i>as he worked his ER shift at the hospital.</i>

189
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:44,667
<i>The bereaved family has been</i>
<i>pursuing legal action</i>

190
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,002
<i>to hold the hospital accountable,</i>

191
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:48,129
<i>and the court issued its ruling today.</i>

192
00:09:48,212 --> 00:09:51,924
<i>In the first trial, the court had ruled</i>
<i>GUMC's favor.</i>

193
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:53,801
<i>The hospital reiterated</i>

194
00:09:53,884 --> 00:09:56,220
<i>it did everything possible</i>
<i>to save Mr. Seo Jin-yeong.</i>

195
00:09:56,887 --> 00:09:59,765
<i>While the bereaved family feels that</i>
<i>the process was handled poorly,</i>

196
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:04,061
<i>the hospital emphasized this result</i>
<i>was due to Seo's medical condition,</i>

197
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:07,189
<i>and not the manner in which</i>
<i>the hospital responded.</i>

198
00:10:08,774 --> 00:10:10,192
Well, Director?

199
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:12,403
Look, the hospital won the case.
Isn't that what matters?

200
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:15,072
Seo Jin-yeong's side has just appealed it.

201
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:16,240
Of course, they did.

202
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:19,994
Director, it's true that Kim Myeong-seop
was in charge when this happened.

203
00:10:20,077 --> 00:10:23,497
We're seeing a downturn in public opinion
now that we've won this case.

204
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:25,583
We need to find a way to handle--

205
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,628
Excuse me.

206
00:10:32,506 --> 00:10:34,508
I didn't have a chance
to throw anything out today.

207
00:10:34,592 --> 00:10:35,760
- I see.
- Um.

208
00:10:36,844 --> 00:10:40,097
Ah, thank you.
Thank you so much, Director.

209
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:43,184
Even though all this is going on,

210
00:10:43,267 --> 00:10:45,645
everyone's taking time to go
on business trips, or to seminars.

211
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:48,481
And now this med school quota
is in the conversation again…

212
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:51,859
should people bring up
going on strike again, know this--

213
00:10:51,942 --> 00:10:53,235
I'll form a picket line first.

214
00:10:54,111 --> 00:10:55,613
You see that we have a staffing issue,

215
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:57,198
yet you're all constantly
abandoning your duties.

216
00:10:57,281 --> 00:10:59,784
Which is why we're not able
to fire Doctor Gye, all right?

217
00:10:59,867 --> 00:11:00,868
Let's just stop this.

218
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:02,036
SUCCESS OR FAILURE…

219
00:11:02,119 --> 00:11:04,246
Where did you even find someone like her?

220
00:11:12,296 --> 00:11:14,423
The hospital's been in a tizzy
over the last few days.

221
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:15,424
And it's all because of her.

222
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:16,926
Uh, Dr. Kim.

223
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:19,011
Doctor Gye Su-jeong
really isn't as difficult

224
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:20,388
as all the rumors make her out to be.

225
00:11:20,971 --> 00:11:22,431
And is she my superior or my subordinate?

226
00:11:22,515 --> 00:11:24,600
What? Uh, I don't know.

227
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:27,186
The distinction matters.

228
00:11:27,269 --> 00:11:29,605
Because I don't get it…
is she like a colleague, or like a pupil?

229
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:32,942
Uh, well I barely know about her either,
but from what I hear…

230
00:11:33,025 --> 00:11:34,402
it sounds like she's kinda both.

231
00:11:34,485 --> 00:11:35,861
Okay… so she's a troublemaker.

232
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:37,238
You have any food?

233
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,781
Dr. Gye, are you okay?

234
00:11:38,864 --> 00:11:40,783
Here, I got your lab coat.

235
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:42,451
Hold on. How long
have you been awake?

236
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:44,328
- A while now.
- What? What'd you hear?

237
00:11:45,579 --> 00:11:48,082
"Who's that? Is he a doctor too?"

238
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:51,252
"He's an intern, but honestly,
he seems more like the village idiot."

239
00:11:51,335 --> 00:11:52,753
You've been awake the whole time.

240
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:55,172
- Hold on, were they talking about me?
- Why'd you just lay there?

241
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:57,133
- Do I seem like a village idiot?
- 'Cause I was still tired.

242
00:11:57,216 --> 00:11:58,300
No, but-- why?

243
00:11:58,384 --> 00:12:00,386
"Village idiot. Smiling Bitch."

244
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:02,054
Those goddamn surgeons.

245
00:12:02,138 --> 00:12:04,640
Dr. Jo Won-jin is "Smiling Bitch"?
Tell me more.

246
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:06,934
Will you tell me which wing
you'll be on for your next rotation?

247
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:08,853
But why, Doctor Kim?

248
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:10,104
Oh--

249
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:12,189
Uh, I'm not so sure
the ER is right for me.

250
00:12:12,273 --> 00:12:14,817
You'll be happier. I think you'll
find your strengths lie elsewhere.

251
00:12:15,609 --> 00:12:17,737
It may be possible
to wake someone who's actually asleep,

252
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:21,073
but it's difficult to wake someone
who's just pretending to be asleep.

253
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:24,201
And it's even harder to teach someone
who pretends to know everything.

254
00:12:24,869 --> 00:12:27,705
In that case, the ideal student
would be someone with an empty head,

255
00:12:27,788 --> 00:12:28,998
like the one on that guy.

256
00:12:29,081 --> 00:12:31,625
She's passing you off,
why'd she have to make a parable?

257
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:33,753
I didn't believe all the rumors initially,
but they seem…

258
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:35,004
The rumors are all true.

259
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:37,381
You have a knack for whispering
loud enough for everyone to hear.

260
00:12:38,382 --> 00:12:40,217
Loud whispers are good, you
lower blood pressure that way.

261
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:41,802
You mean it? I'll have
to let the patients know.

262
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:44,388
From what I've heard today,

263
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:45,973
you should give whispering a shot.

264
00:12:46,056 --> 00:12:48,225
Always yelling at people
is bad for your health.

265
00:12:50,853 --> 00:12:52,021
It's a pleasure. Kim Seong-jin.

266
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:53,439
My name's Gye Su-jeong.

267
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:55,524
Park Tae-gyeong is my name.

268
00:12:59,987 --> 00:13:02,573
<i>...on Guseo University Medical Center,</i>
<i>and EMT Seo Jin-yeong,</i>

269
00:13:02,656 --> 00:13:04,116
<i>- who tragically died</i>…
- Hello, Dr. Bae.

270
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,242
- People.
- Hello, Dr. Bae.

271
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:08,871
All right, you guys, don't sweat it,
you can keep watching.

272
00:13:08,954 --> 00:13:11,165
No need to act all super-secret.
C'mon, you can put it on.

273
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:13,626
With the allegations,
and the investigation…

274
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:16,796
you've really been going through a lot,
but you've made it through one hurdle.

275
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:19,006
Well that, I don't know…
They'll appeal it soon.

276
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:21,884
Dr. Kim Seong-jin really hasn't
changed at all, has he?

277
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,677
You don't think he'll side against us
in the case, do you?

278
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:25,095
I don't see any reason he would.

279
00:13:25,805 --> 00:13:27,932
I mean, just being caught
in-between like he is,

280
00:13:28,015 --> 00:13:31,393
in his perspective, I'm sure it's
totally been gnawing away at the guy.

281
00:13:34,104 --> 00:13:36,565
Hey, why aren't you checking
your texts? What's going on?

282
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:40,611
Hey. This isn't gonna do.
I can't open up an OR right now.

283
00:13:40,694 --> 00:13:42,488
Why not? We have to
get the surgery done now.

284
00:13:42,571 --> 00:13:44,865
I can't, no way. Let's
reevaluate the patient.

285
00:13:45,574 --> 00:13:46,659
- Hello.
- Hey.

286
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:49,245
Oh, hey, uh…
sorry about earlier this morning.

287
00:13:49,995 --> 00:13:51,622
And thank you for calling me, too.

288
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:53,541
Why are you alone?

289
00:13:53,624 --> 00:13:56,043
Dr. Gye Su-jeong's working
in the emergency room right now.

290
00:13:56,126 --> 00:13:58,045
What? On whose orders?

291
00:14:01,131 --> 00:14:02,716
Is stationing just a joke to you?

292
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,009
What the hell is going on?

293
00:14:04,093 --> 00:14:07,346
Director Bu sent her there temporarily,
because the ER needed a hand.

294
00:14:07,429 --> 00:14:09,890
How is a surgeon in the ER
good for General Surgery?

295
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:11,892
Let's see, our wondrous new intern.

296
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:13,602
You came to get your stuff, right?

297
00:14:14,186 --> 00:14:16,564
Here. Why don't we get going?
Have a nice day, Dr. Jo.

298
00:14:20,484 --> 00:14:22,862
Even kids get punished when they
bully someone. What're you thinking?

299
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:24,738
Why're you trying to meddle
all of a sudden?

300
00:14:24,822 --> 00:14:26,115
Go back and get me in that OR.

301
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:28,325
Who's accountable
if they die on the table, huh?

302
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:31,245
I don't allow high-risk operations,
you know that.

303
00:14:31,328 --> 00:14:32,329
Find someone else.

304
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:34,790
Then how else can I get an OR?

305
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:41,714
I'm a busy man,
but for the future of Korean medicine,

306
00:14:41,797 --> 00:14:43,007
I'll give you two minutes
of one-on-one time.

307
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:46,760
Dr. Kim Seong-jin talked about
an EMT named Seo this morning.

308
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:49,263
Is he the person on the news
who died of a subarachnoid hemorrhage

309
00:14:49,346 --> 00:14:50,681
while working at the hospital last year?

310
00:14:50,764 --> 00:14:52,308
Mm-hmm. What else?

311
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:54,101
I heard the doctors who could do
a craniotomy weren't here,

312
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:55,102
so is that why he died?

313
00:14:55,185 --> 00:14:57,187
You're partially right, but mostly wrong.

314
00:14:58,564 --> 00:15:01,025
Then, would Dr. Kim Seong-jin or Dr. Bae…

315
00:15:01,108 --> 00:15:03,235
as they're the ones who did
the coil embolization, be--

316
00:15:03,319 --> 00:15:05,613
ENDOVASCULAR COILING: A TREATMENT
THAT DOESN'T REQUIRE CRANIOTOMY

317
00:15:05,696 --> 00:15:07,656
No. They both did all that they could.

318
00:15:09,116 --> 00:15:11,160
<i>In fact, Dr. Kim Seong-jin wasn't even</i>
<i>on call that day.</i>

319
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:16,790
<i>On his way out, after an all-nighter,</i>
<i>he found EMT Seo Jin-yeong unconscious.</i>

320
00:15:16,874 --> 00:15:18,626
<i>He was slumped over the ER desk,</i>

321
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:20,961
<i>- so everyone thought he was sleeping.</i>
- EMT Seo?

322
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:23,631
<i>The ER was slammed earlier that morning</i>
<i>because of a major car accident</i>

323
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:25,716
Over here! I need help over here!

324
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:29,637
Seo! Seo, wake up, buddy! Can you hear me?

325
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:31,597
- Hurry up. Keep moving!
- Come on.

326
00:15:35,225 --> 00:15:36,769
Dr. Bae, let's get going.

327
00:15:36,852 --> 00:15:37,728
This man needs your help,

328
00:15:37,811 --> 00:15:40,272
or are we gonna let him die
while the both of us just stand here?

329
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:42,566
This place has ten neurosurgeons,

330
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,318
are you saying none of 'em
can treat a brain hemorrhage?

331
00:15:44,401 --> 00:15:46,403
He has an excessive amount
of intracranial pressure.

332
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:49,323
And with the location of the aneurysm,
clipping is the answer,

333
00:15:49,406 --> 00:15:51,283
- though by now…
- Then let's page somebody right now.

334
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:52,910
The doctors who can do
the procedure aren't here.

335
00:15:52,993 --> 00:15:54,244
How are they both not--

336
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:58,457
Forget those two, Dr. Bae Heung-gon…

337
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,668
you and I should do
a coil emboilization first.

338
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:03,295
We have no time to lose.
I'll find a place to transfer him.

339
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:05,214
- I get it, but…
- Hey, Bae Heung-gon!

340
00:16:07,007 --> 00:16:09,134
Listen, I'm begging, do the right thing.

341
00:16:09,885 --> 00:16:11,637
EMT Seo has worked here for ten years.

342
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:15,057
He's here at this hospital every day,
he least we can do is try our best--

343
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:18,852
I think that is the
least we can do, isn't it?

344
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:20,270
ANGIOGRAPHY SUITE 3

345
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:26,235
There's no way. It's too far in there.
A coil embolization wouldn't do anything.

346
00:16:26,318 --> 00:16:29,405
- Call the attendings one more--
- One is in Naju for a funeral,

347
00:16:29,488 --> 00:16:31,782
the other's in Germany for training.

348
00:16:31,865 --> 00:16:33,200
Then I'll transfer him as fast as I can.

349
00:16:33,283 --> 00:16:35,619
Dr. Nam said they'd be able to treat him
at Junggyeong. Thanks.

350
00:16:35,703 --> 00:16:38,455
His intracranial pressure is too high!
There's nothing we can do!

351
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:41,375
<i>They transferred him to Junggyeong</i>
<i>University Hospital, but he died anyway.</i>

352
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:45,754
His intracranial pressure was too high,
so even if they had tried the procedure,

353
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:47,840
the chances of it succeeding
weren't high at all.

354
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:50,009
That's the one part you got wrong,
and the crux of the lawsuit.

355
00:16:50,092 --> 00:16:51,093
Now, I gotta head in there.

356
00:16:52,052 --> 00:16:53,679
When you say the chances were
low that the surgery would work…

357
00:16:55,139 --> 00:16:56,223
what's your rationale?

358
00:16:56,306 --> 00:16:58,308
That he was destined to die
no matter what they tried on him?

359
00:16:58,392 --> 00:17:01,186
Basically, it's the patient's fault?
Is that it?

360
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:03,313
That isn't the type of
thing a doctor should be saying.

361
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:05,107
Then, what am I supposed to say?

362
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:06,734
"Sorry, I couldn't save the patient.

363
00:17:06,817 --> 00:17:09,278
Please, haul me to prison,
so sorry about that." That what you want?

364
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:11,947
Doctors have our limits, we're only human.

365
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:14,700
Had there been one other doctor
who could do a craniotomy clipping,

366
00:17:14,783 --> 00:17:16,243
I would've taken every chance
on that possibility--

367
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:17,703
Hippocrates really got to you, huh?

368
00:17:18,495 --> 00:17:20,622
Years ago, if a doctor did that surgery,
people would go,

369
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:22,541
"wow, he's got God's hands, doesn't he?"

370
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:25,502
Going four hours at least, bent over,
staring through a tiny little microscope,

371
00:17:25,586 --> 00:17:27,588
and poking around a patient's bloody brain

372
00:17:27,671 --> 00:17:30,174
Fine, let's say you muscle through it all,
and the surgery is a success--

373
00:17:30,257 --> 00:17:31,425
know what the shitty part really is?

374
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:33,469
That clip could slip off at any time.

375
00:17:34,094 --> 00:17:35,804
If the aneurysm ruptures,
the patient's either dead,

376
00:17:35,888 --> 00:17:37,514
or disabled for life. Who takes the blame?

377
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:41,060
Do you know how many medical lawsuits
come from this surgery?

378
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:42,478
And those clips are pricy to get.

379
00:17:43,103 --> 00:17:45,064
You know the reimbursement rate
on a six person surgery

380
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:46,106
barely covers the overhead. Get it?

381
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:50,736
The next time you wanna tell me
what a doctor's supposed to say,

382
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:52,988
learn how to do a craniotomy first.

383
00:17:53,572 --> 00:17:54,448
You do those.

384
00:17:55,407 --> 00:17:57,201
I'm going to learn coiling from Dr. Bae.

385
00:17:57,284 --> 00:17:59,703
It comes with lower risk, takes less staff
because it's non-surgical,

386
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,163
and there's actual money in doing it.

387
00:18:01,246 --> 00:18:02,498
That's where I draw my line.

388
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:04,792
Stick to what I know I can handle.

389
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:10,881
So, am I not a doctor because of that?
What do you think?

390
00:18:11,465 --> 00:18:13,801
Huh? Huh?

391
00:18:17,262 --> 00:18:20,099
Mister Eung-gu said if you hit someone,

392
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:22,226
and you aim for that pressure point,
like I just did,

393
00:18:22,309 --> 00:18:25,062
then they'll either die,
or end up disabled for life.

394
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:29,191
"When cerebral aneurysms rupture.

395
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:31,401
one patient out of three
will die instantly.

396
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:32,986
One in three will die
on the way to the hospital.

397
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:35,656
Only that remaining one in three patients

398
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:38,033
can actually get to a hospital
in time for a surgery."

399
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:42,412
You had a patient who was lucky enough
to have been in that last one-third,

400
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:44,498
and beyond that,
he was in the hospital already.

401
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:47,459
That chance doesn't factor into
how you see it?

402
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:49,253
I guess you don't care
if a patient dies on the table

403
00:18:49,336 --> 00:18:51,088
'cause you threw 'em into surgery
based on that chance.

404
00:18:51,171 --> 00:18:52,923
Dr. Ma, what are you doing here?

405
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:54,091
Get ready and get inside.

406
00:18:54,174 --> 00:18:57,719
Didn't you wanna get certified
in GS and NS like Dr. Bae?

407
00:18:57,803 --> 00:18:59,555
Do you expect another residency like this?

408
00:19:00,848 --> 00:19:02,266
To be frank, at your skill level…

409
00:19:02,349 --> 00:19:04,977
you'd probably get sued
even just doing non-surgical things.

410
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:06,854
Better go in and get
some more practice in.

411
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:09,231
Get in there, resident.

412
00:19:18,448 --> 00:19:19,783
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

413
00:19:20,784 --> 00:19:23,704
I feel like I'm forever putting out fires
that you've started.

414
00:19:23,787 --> 00:19:24,788
But please correct me if I'm wrong here.

415
00:19:24,872 --> 00:19:29,251
No, that's certainly true. However,
I didn't start this particular fire.

416
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:32,087
Uh, I actually started it. This is on me.

417
00:19:32,171 --> 00:19:34,089
I crossed the line
and spoke out of turn with Dr. Ma.

418
00:19:35,048 --> 00:19:35,883
I sincerely apologize.

419
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:40,012
Don't annoy anyone going into my OR
within 30 minutes before the operation.

420
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:41,847
It's distracting.

421
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:46,143
- We're 31 minutes and 20 seconds out.
- God, I swear…

422
00:19:46,226 --> 00:19:48,270
Dr. Gye, don't.
It's bad enough, let's just stay quiet.

423
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:51,440
They shouldn't let you two
work together, seriously. Ugh.

424
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:59,573
You could've observed the surgery,
but because of me…

425
00:20:01,283 --> 00:20:02,784
You weren't the reason I didn't.

426
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,661
Someone called me and
asked to get together.

427
00:20:04,745 --> 00:20:08,665
When someone calls to meet up suddenly,
you actually do? That's surprising.

428
00:20:10,334 --> 00:20:11,501
I brought you this.

429
00:20:12,377 --> 00:20:13,879
They give you these when you donate blood.

430
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:16,423
Wish I could donate every morning.

431
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:19,176
Don't you dare do it every day,
don't you dare!

432
00:20:19,259 --> 00:20:21,261
What, do you wanna let 'em take
your spinal fluid while you're at it, too?

433
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:22,971
Wait, what are you doing? Who are you?

434
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:25,557
That's Ms. Jang.

435
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:26,767
The Ms. Jang?

436
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:27,935
Wait, you mean that lady?

437
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:30,520
- The one who has you doing free work?
- What are you saying?

438
00:20:31,438 --> 00:20:35,317
I donated blood, I worked all day long…
I'm brutally exhausted.

439
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,818
So, Miss Jang, cook me
something good when we get home.

440
00:20:36,902 --> 00:20:40,280
If you could just mind your business,
they would handle it.

441
00:20:40,781 --> 00:20:42,282
I've been telling you
to lay low, haven't I?

442
00:20:42,366 --> 00:20:44,284
Hey, Dr. Gye was
incredible in surgery today.

443
00:20:44,368 --> 00:20:45,744
But she shouldn't be incredible, she--

444
00:20:47,746 --> 00:20:50,332
You should feel things out more,
do a big surgery, then another,

445
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:51,875
and focus on making money.

446
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:54,795
Why are you working
down in Emergency? Huh?

447
00:20:54,878 --> 00:20:56,922
Then you can't do more surgeries.
I can't make money.

448
00:20:57,714 --> 00:20:59,883
Just lay low until you get back
to the GS depar…

449
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:02,427
Oh, my goodness!

450
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:05,138
Oh, Doctor… I'm so sorry! I can't believe
I was so rude in front of you, Doctor.

451
00:21:05,222 --> 00:21:07,599
- Oh, I'm so sorry, my goodness!
- Oh, don't worry, it's fine.

452
00:21:08,308 --> 00:21:10,018
I'm just an intern, ma'am.
My name is Park Tae-gyeong.

453
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:13,522
Oh, okay… Ah, well then, hello!
Now, where were we?

454
00:21:13,605 --> 00:21:16,358
I'm Director of the first
doctor-for-hire agency in Korea.

455
00:21:16,441 --> 00:21:17,943
Jang Hui-suk, nice to meet you.

456
00:21:18,568 --> 00:21:21,947
You might say that I'm essentially
Dr. Gye Su-jeong's agent.

457
00:21:22,531 --> 00:21:25,450
Since you might be a client or employee

458
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:27,244
that may come to work with us one day,

459
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:29,204
please take this, Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

460
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:30,330
DIRECTOR JANG HUI-SUK

461
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:32,541
That sounds great, but right now,
I'm just an intern, not a doctor.

462
00:21:32,624 --> 00:21:35,002
Oh no, enough with that--
Of course you are!

463
00:21:35,085 --> 00:21:37,212
With all you've studied,
and the devotion you've put into it.

464
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:42,384
Ah, I'm horribly thirsty.
Here, can you grab some drinks, Su-jeong?

465
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:43,510
One for the doctor, and one for me.

466
00:21:43,593 --> 00:21:45,762
- Oh no, I can go do that, allow me.
- Oh, no, no, no way.

467
00:21:45,846 --> 00:21:47,681
Sit down, Doctor. Su-jeong.

468
00:21:48,432 --> 00:21:50,767
Just by looking at your face, Doctor,
I can tell

469
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:53,228
that there are other great doctors
in your family, aren't there?

470
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:54,396
Oh, how did you know?

471
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:03,405
Hello, Miss. Excuse me, Miss.

472
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:05,115
Oh, you need something?

473
00:22:05,198 --> 00:22:08,327
Yes, sorry, uh… I was
wondering if you have an extra tissue?

474
00:22:09,578 --> 00:22:13,623
Yes, sure, I have a moist wipe,
not for sticky stuff though,

475
00:22:13,707 --> 00:22:14,541
it'll make a mess. Here, use this.

476
00:22:15,959 --> 00:22:17,419
There you go.

477
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:22,758
Whoa… you're right. Thank you very much.

478
00:22:24,051 --> 00:22:26,428
I don’t believe you and I met.
Which wing are you?

479
00:22:29,681 --> 00:22:31,266
I work here and there.

480
00:22:31,767 --> 00:22:33,643
I'm more like a contractor.
In that category.

481
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:37,105
I also work on contract, as a cleaner.
So, I also work all over.

482
00:22:37,189 --> 00:22:39,399
Oh… That'd make you my senior.

483
00:22:39,483 --> 00:22:42,152
Ah, gosh, no, I'm no senior.
Have a good one.

484
00:22:46,281 --> 00:22:47,657
Miss, are you doing alright?

485
00:22:47,741 --> 00:22:49,326
Ah, I'm sorry.
Just a headache, that's all.

486
00:22:49,951 --> 00:22:51,161
Is this the first time it's bothered you?

487
00:22:51,244 --> 00:22:53,288
You know how it can be.

488
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:56,124
It's true there's a different pain
every day when you're old.

489
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:59,169
Ah, no. Don't--

490
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:05,467
Okay, well… thank you for
the drink, have a good day.

491
00:23:11,390 --> 00:23:14,810
I think a part of Dr. Kim Seong-jin
believes the whole thing was his fault,

492
00:23:14,893 --> 00:23:16,228
which is why he's taking it so hard.

493
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:19,314
When it got out,
the security footage caused quite a stir.

494
00:23:19,398 --> 00:23:23,151
EMT Seo there, slumped over that desk
in the ER, just laying there all alone.

495
00:23:23,235 --> 00:23:25,821
I saw that too. It really makes you think,

496
00:23:25,904 --> 00:23:28,865
Is there anyone in this place
that would notice it at all

497
00:23:28,949 --> 00:23:30,784
if I were the one laying there,
slumped over?

498
00:23:30,867 --> 00:23:33,453
- That's why everyone was so upset.
- Yes.

499
00:23:33,537 --> 00:23:36,581
How does a video like that
get released to the public?

500
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:38,792
Uhm… well, I think
someone leaked the video

501
00:23:38,875 --> 00:23:39,876
Oh, wow…

502
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:42,045
And so, the hospital administrators
called in all the nurses and EMTs

503
00:23:42,129 --> 00:23:44,673
to come and answer questions
about what happened,

504
00:23:44,756 --> 00:23:46,675
and they never really figured out
who the leak was.

505
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:48,385
Ahh… except, the doctors
weren't interviewed?

506
00:23:48,468 --> 00:23:50,053
Well, they never found out
who really did it,

507
00:23:50,137 --> 00:23:51,388
but protests were organized

508
00:23:51,471 --> 00:23:53,098
by the Union of Korean Health
and Medical Workers.

509
00:23:53,181 --> 00:23:55,142
Goodness, that must
have traumatized everyone.

510
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:59,354
Oh, my. I can't believe I'm using
such a fancy word

511
00:23:59,438 --> 00:24:00,272
in front of you, Doctor, I'm sorry.

512
00:24:04,776 --> 00:24:05,735
Come on…

513
00:24:06,611 --> 00:24:08,155
Are you gonna drink that or not?

514
00:24:08,238 --> 00:24:11,366
Remember the words of the son
of a great director who started with

515
00:24:11,450 --> 00:24:13,076
a plastic surgery clinic in Busan,

516
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:15,537
and grew it into
the biggest medical center of the region.

517
00:24:16,496 --> 00:24:20,917
Her grip slipped off both objects,
the can and the wet wipe…

518
00:24:25,797 --> 00:24:28,008
I gotta say,
I really like this time of day.

519
00:24:28,091 --> 00:24:30,010
We quietly collect everything
that happened on our shifts,

520
00:24:30,010 --> 00:24:32,095
writing up a document,
letting our coworkers know about it,

521
00:24:32,179 --> 00:24:34,055
and then we get ready to go.

522
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:36,183
- Who's going?
- Dr. Gye.

523
00:24:38,518 --> 00:24:40,312
If you've got any big questions,
right now'd be the moment to ask.

524
00:24:40,395 --> 00:24:41,521
It's nearly time.

525
00:24:44,274 --> 00:24:46,485
So, how did you know

526
00:24:46,568 --> 00:24:48,904
that her chest pain was really just
acid reflux caused by GERD?

527
00:24:49,905 --> 00:24:51,865
<i>Ms. Ha Mi-ju, 61 years old.</i>

528
00:24:51,948 --> 00:24:54,951
Now, I see here that she's complaining
of severe chest pain,

529
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:57,412
however her test results
are completely normal.

530
00:24:57,496 --> 00:25:00,081
You presented with the same symptoms
once before, in the early morning?

531
00:25:00,165 --> 00:25:03,210
She wakes from the pain.
It's especially bad at night.

532
00:25:03,293 --> 00:25:07,005
I see, then... Miss Ha, let me
have another listen to your chest.

533
00:25:07,088 --> 00:25:10,091
I've got a question for you.
Have you eaten anything today?

534
00:25:10,842 --> 00:25:11,968
No.

535
00:25:14,596 --> 00:25:15,680
Miss Ha, forgive me,

536
00:25:15,764 --> 00:25:19,267
but do you regularly drink coffee,
and eat foods with a lot of grease?

537
00:25:19,351 --> 00:25:20,268
Yes.

538
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:22,521
I'm gonna press your abdomen for a moment.
Slowly. okay, and--

539
00:25:23,396 --> 00:25:25,190
- Does that hurt here?
- Yes, it hurts.

540
00:25:27,108 --> 00:25:30,487
<i>The ambiguous placement of her hand,</i>
<i>and the area where she swept her hand</i>

541
00:25:30,570 --> 00:25:31,571
<i>when she gestured as well.</i>

542
00:25:33,156 --> 00:25:34,199
What an amazing description.

543
00:25:34,282 --> 00:25:35,742
Could I put that in the chart, you think?

544
00:25:35,825 --> 00:25:36,993
Yeah, you can write as you'd like.

545
00:25:37,661 --> 00:25:39,913
I spent years in a place
where I didn't know the language,

546
00:25:39,996 --> 00:25:43,208
so I had no choice but to focus
on the patient's attitude and behavior.

547
00:25:44,501 --> 00:25:47,087
But why did the patient choose
that way to describe it to you?

548
00:25:47,170 --> 00:25:48,713
That's how it goes
with patients sometimes.

549
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:50,840
That's why doctors need
to ask the right questions.

550
00:25:51,383 --> 00:25:55,470
Like today, my head was all over
the place, so I missed a few things.

551
00:25:56,388 --> 00:25:59,266
It's extremely rare
that a patient is in pain

552
00:26:00,892 --> 00:26:03,937
and capable of articulating it.

553
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:06,231
You're right on that.

554
00:26:06,314 --> 00:26:09,693
I'm used to doctors saying don't interfere
with care or I didn't ask for criticism

555
00:26:09,776 --> 00:26:10,986
and reacting all offended.

556
00:26:11,695 --> 00:26:15,073
Well, I got to say your self-awareness
is really refreshing.

557
00:26:15,156 --> 00:26:17,993
Okay, on that note, why don't we all grab
some late-night snacks together.

558
00:26:18,076 --> 00:26:19,077
Have a good night.

559
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:20,579
Wait, you're going home?

560
00:26:20,662 --> 00:26:23,582
Seriously, Dr. Park, is she seriously
going back home now this early?

561
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:25,250
Yeah.

562
00:26:40,724 --> 00:26:42,642
Uh, lock in Tae-gyeong.

563
00:26:48,940 --> 00:26:51,109
Oh gross. Now it's all lukewarm.

564
00:26:55,947 --> 00:26:58,825
Dr. Gye, are you okay?
Here, I've got your lab coat.

565
00:26:58,908 --> 00:27:00,368
Hold on. How long have you been awake?

566
00:27:03,079 --> 00:27:04,414
Her name was all smudged.

567
00:27:05,874 --> 00:27:07,375
Uh.

568
00:27:08,668 --> 00:27:09,961
I ought to make her a new one.

569
00:27:25,894 --> 00:27:28,521
Just judging by what I've seen of Dr. Gye.

570
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:32,317
The day she gets a lab coat
with her name embroidered...

571
00:27:36,404 --> 00:27:39,074
Okay, well, I should give her
some extras just in case.

572
00:28:02,013 --> 00:28:04,516
You skipped dinner again, didn't you?

573
00:28:06,351 --> 00:28:07,394
Thank you.

574
00:28:08,395 --> 00:28:12,232
So I've been listening to the EMTs that
are in charge of getting patients here.

575
00:28:12,315 --> 00:28:15,610
They're always saying to each other,
on the first floor at Guseo in Kyungi,

576
00:28:15,694 --> 00:28:16,695
no one gets turned away.

577
00:28:17,862 --> 00:28:20,073
They put a good doctor there
who cares a whole lot.

578
00:28:20,990 --> 00:28:23,952
I guess I'm saying stop getting angry
and saying you'll quit soon.

579
00:28:24,035 --> 00:28:26,496
You'll be all right. Just hang in there.

580
00:28:26,579 --> 00:28:30,208
So that my kid can come visit her dad
at work, meet a good doctor like you,

581
00:28:30,291 --> 00:28:32,001
and say she wants to be a doctor too.

582
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:37,841
Go on, eat, it'll get mushy.

583
00:28:48,226 --> 00:28:49,811
Hello ma'am, how are you doing?

584
00:28:50,770 --> 00:28:53,690
Seo Jin-yeong and I
used to work at the same hospital.

585
00:29:10,623 --> 00:29:13,793
We're seeing the same thing, right?
We're not just both imagining it?

586
00:29:13,877 --> 00:29:17,338
Yep, and we're looking
at the same thing we saw yesterday.

587
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:24,095
Hi, uh, Dr. Gye.

588
00:29:25,263 --> 00:29:29,726
Dr. Gye Su-jeong, are you pretending to be
asleep again, or are you actually asleep?

589
00:29:29,809 --> 00:29:31,978
No, I think she's really asleep.

590
00:29:32,061 --> 00:29:34,564
Wait, why is she sleeping here,
not the on-call room like the rest of us?

591
00:29:34,647 --> 00:29:36,733
I don't get it.
Didn't she leave right at 6 yesterday?

592
00:29:36,816 --> 00:29:37,817
Yeah.

593
00:29:38,651 --> 00:29:41,654
Dr. Gye, come on. Dr. Gye, Dr. Gye.

594
00:29:42,447 --> 00:29:44,157
Good morning. Did you sleep all right?

595
00:29:47,243 --> 00:29:51,039
Oh, man,
these firm hospital beds are perfect.

596
00:29:51,122 --> 00:29:52,499
I slept like a rock.

597
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:56,252
Are you actually being serious right now?
Do we need this bed for anything?

598
00:29:56,336 --> 00:29:58,546
This is for patients
to receive treatment or to wait

599
00:29:58,630 --> 00:29:59,798
until we can tend to their care.

600
00:29:59,881 --> 00:30:00,590
Okay?

601
00:30:00,673 --> 00:30:02,801
Just be glad we didn't have a rush,
an emergency.

602
00:30:02,967 --> 00:30:04,302
So no patients are here who need it.

603
00:30:04,385 --> 00:30:05,136
No, but that wasn't my--

604
00:30:05,220 --> 00:30:06,763
Did you not go home yesterday?

605
00:30:07,388 --> 00:30:08,932
Yeah, and then today I came in early. Oh.

606
00:30:16,481 --> 00:30:17,857
What are you waiting on someone?

607
00:30:18,942 --> 00:30:23,488
Ah, so I still don't have to clock in yet.
Well then I suppose...

608
00:30:25,657 --> 00:30:27,075
What--

609
00:30:36,584 --> 00:30:38,753
Oh, hello, Dr. Jo.

610
00:30:38,837 --> 00:30:41,172
You pull an all-nighter. Pick something.

611
00:30:41,256 --> 00:30:43,633
Uh, no thanks, I'm all right,
not really too hungry.

612
00:30:48,513 --> 00:30:49,722
Shopping for groceries.

613
00:31:00,483 --> 00:31:02,443
Oh well, I'm more awake now.

614
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:06,614
Been talking at all to Dr. Ma recently?

615
00:31:06,698 --> 00:31:10,451
Nope, not at all.
Did the surgery that day go all right?

616
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:12,787
Well, Bae's a good teacher,
so he just did as he said.

617
00:31:12,871 --> 00:31:14,330
Oh, I'm glad.

618
00:31:15,081 --> 00:31:17,333
I was scared he might have struggled
keeping focus because of me.

619
00:31:17,417 --> 00:31:19,586
Well, his temper's not the greatest,
but he does his job.

620
00:31:21,504 --> 00:31:23,089
So out of the interns,
you're the outsider.

621
00:31:23,256 --> 00:31:24,048
Outsider?

622
00:31:24,132 --> 00:31:26,259
No, no, I'm not an outsider.
I've got friends.

623
00:31:26,342 --> 00:31:27,343
Oh yeah, who?

624
00:31:28,970 --> 00:31:30,138
Well, I went to high school with them.

625
00:31:31,472 --> 00:31:35,894
Oh, you know what it's like.
The interns are pretty busy here.

626
00:31:35,977 --> 00:31:37,770
Well, actually,
the interns in our department

627
00:31:37,854 --> 00:31:39,522
go to social gatherings and eat together.

628
00:31:40,523 --> 00:31:42,400
Oh, that's good for them.

629
00:31:43,610 --> 00:31:45,361
I just want to focus
on studying for a specialty.

630
00:31:48,156 --> 00:31:49,532
That's what happens when you lie.

631
00:31:52,493 --> 00:31:54,454
That why you're worried about Dr. Gye,
because she's also an outsider?

632
00:31:54,537 --> 00:31:57,874
What? No, I don't think either one of us
are really outsiders.

633
00:31:57,957 --> 00:32:01,210
You can't do a surgery single-handed.
You need others to rely on.

634
00:32:01,294 --> 00:32:03,504
You need to know how to work
and get along with others.

635
00:32:03,588 --> 00:32:07,342
There's a time to pause your emotions
and smile despite how pissed you are.

636
00:32:07,425 --> 00:32:10,261
Mm, I know that technique,
a smiling bitch.

637
00:32:10,345 --> 00:32:11,888
How'd you know I had hypotension, huh?

638
00:32:12,805 --> 00:32:14,807
You have a way
of raising stress levels, intern.

639
00:32:15,433 --> 00:32:16,434
This tastes great, Dr. Jo.

640
00:32:16,434 --> 00:32:17,435
Here, you should have a little bit.

641
00:32:17,477 --> 00:32:20,563
The reason I bought it was because I
pitied you village idiot.

642
00:32:20,647 --> 00:32:21,856
For real? Well, I had no idea.

643
00:32:24,484 --> 00:32:27,695
Oh, actually, um,
there's a question I'd like to ask you.

644
00:32:28,446 --> 00:32:31,491
In this hospital we have 10 doctors
working in neurosurgery, and if they

645
00:32:31,574 --> 00:32:35,745
say they can't do a craniotomy,
well, we have no shortage of beds here.

646
00:32:35,828 --> 00:32:37,664
Why not hire more doctors who can do one?

647
00:32:37,747 --> 00:32:39,540
It's all about the money.

648
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:43,252
Do you think there are more patients with
appendicitis or with brain hemorrhages?

649
00:32:43,336 --> 00:32:46,297
Both are cheap to handle,
so why do the harder surgery then?

650
00:32:46,464 --> 00:32:47,924
The more they do, the more they lose.

651
00:32:48,007 --> 00:32:49,801
They focus on the surgeries
that make money.

652
00:32:49,884 --> 00:32:53,304
There are hospitals nearby
who have less than 1000 beds to go around,

653
00:32:53,471 --> 00:32:55,515
but they've got more doctors
capable of treating a brain.

654
00:32:55,598 --> 00:32:58,393
Kindly too, I mean,
you can't help but compare them.

655
00:32:58,476 --> 00:33:00,979
I get it now.
So then that's why you said that.

656
00:33:01,521 --> 00:33:05,525
Of course a solely moneymaking hospital
like the one they're running is bound

657
00:33:05,608 --> 00:33:07,485
to have some major structural issues.

658
00:33:07,568 --> 00:33:10,196
In fact, I'm incredibly good
at sniffing out things.

659
00:33:10,279 --> 00:33:12,365
Oh right, then, if you're so good
at sniffing out things,

660
00:33:12,490 --> 00:33:15,159
then why couldn't you sniff out
this flat tire before we all got stuck?

661
00:33:16,077 --> 00:33:20,206
Because these flat tires smell like shit.
It's terrible.

662
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:25,294
What are you looking at?

663
00:33:27,296 --> 00:33:30,008
How many doctors can do
a craniotomy clipping in Korea?

664
00:33:30,717 --> 00:33:35,054
Right now, barely over 130 in total, and
most of them in their sixties by now too.

665
00:33:35,722 --> 00:33:38,516
To that end, there aren't many people who
teach it and few people who want to learn.

666
00:33:38,599 --> 00:33:40,268
It's on the verge of going extinct.

667
00:33:41,436 --> 00:33:43,730
All right, but there are cases
where a craniotomy clipping is the only

668
00:33:43,813 --> 00:33:45,440
technique that can resolve the issue.

669
00:33:45,523 --> 00:33:46,691
So what do we do then?

670
00:33:59,162 --> 00:34:03,166
Are you all right?
Hello, miss, are you okay?

671
00:34:04,542 --> 00:34:07,253
Can you get up for me a moment, ma'am?
Just a moment.

672
00:34:07,336 --> 00:34:08,588
Are you okay?

673
00:34:10,381 --> 00:34:13,301
EMT Seo, are you okay? EMT Seo!

674
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:17,680
In that situation,
you hope one of those 130 brain surgeons

675
00:34:17,764 --> 00:34:19,474
is at the hospital that day.

676
00:34:20,016 --> 00:34:24,103
Hey, over here, over here. Quick,
over here, I need help with this patient.

677
00:34:49,045 --> 00:34:51,130
Could Dr. Hwang get here fast?
It'd take him 40 to 50 minutes.

678
00:34:51,214 --> 00:34:53,424
He's in his hole at the KMA
and the highway's backed up.

679
00:34:53,508 --> 00:34:55,802
And Jang,
his conference ended yesterday, correct?

680
00:34:56,385 --> 00:34:58,763
Uh, he's preoccupied. He's sightseeing.

681
00:34:58,846 --> 00:35:01,724
He took his whole family to Ulsan.
He'll be back as quick as he can.

682
00:35:01,808 --> 00:35:03,893
Family man, Dr. Jang.
Well, isn't that just great?

683
00:35:04,477 --> 00:35:05,937
What the hell, right? This is bad.

684
00:35:10,274 --> 00:35:12,610
It's an SAH caused by an aneurysm rupture.

685
00:35:12,693 --> 00:35:14,112
Why not coiling? It'd be hard.

686
00:35:14,278 --> 00:35:16,989
And even if we did, we'd have to wait.
She's conscious right now.

687
00:35:17,073 --> 00:35:20,201
She's in pain and suffering through
seizures, but she is still conscious.

688
00:35:20,284 --> 00:35:21,202
Well, let's move her.

689
00:35:21,285 --> 00:35:22,745
Under no circumstance.

690
00:35:22,829 --> 00:35:24,789
We have to treat the patient here.
That's the only option.

691
00:35:24,872 --> 00:35:27,208
You've seen yourself, Ms. Lee.
There's nobody here who can operate.

692
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:29,085
Then we'll hold out
for Drs. Hwang and Jang.

693
00:35:29,168 --> 00:35:30,962
What? Why would we do that?

694
00:35:31,045 --> 00:35:33,714
Another Guseo employee
collapsed this year, and we did nothing.

695
00:35:34,507 --> 00:35:38,302
If she ends up dying in our hospital,
we won't be able to control the situation.

696
00:35:38,386 --> 00:35:42,056
If she waits it out, she'll die too.
I don't know much about medicine,

697
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:46,018
but I do know that the closest location
that can handle this procedure

698
00:35:46,102 --> 00:35:48,521
that's trained in clipping
and could take on this operation

699
00:35:48,604 --> 00:35:51,107
would be Daeseok Hospital,
50 minutes away.

700
00:35:51,190 --> 00:35:52,108
Wait, what are you saying?

701
00:35:52,191 --> 00:35:54,235
Dr. Nam's at Joonggyeong University,
20 minutes east.

702
00:35:54,318 --> 00:35:57,655
Dr. Nam has opened his own practice.
He quit because things got too tough.

703
00:35:57,738 --> 00:35:58,739
Shit.

704
00:36:00,324 --> 00:36:03,119
Considering the heavy morning traffic,
it'll take an hour to get there,

705
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:04,287
even in an ambulance.

706
00:36:04,370 --> 00:36:06,080
If she stays or gets sent out,
it'll be the same.

707
00:36:06,247 --> 00:36:08,666
We're running out of time.
We need to get ready to transfer now.

708
00:36:08,749 --> 00:36:10,585
Let Daeseok know
we can't handle this here.

709
00:36:10,668 --> 00:36:12,503
There's a doctor
who can handle the operation.

710
00:36:13,796 --> 00:36:14,797
And who is that?

711
00:36:17,008 --> 00:36:18,759
I would call on Director Bu Seung-gwon.

712
00:36:20,386 --> 00:36:23,139
I've studied a lot of material
about your great skills

713
00:36:23,222 --> 00:36:24,807
and about your past operations.

714
00:36:24,891 --> 00:36:26,225
Please, I beg of you.

715
00:36:27,727 --> 00:36:30,313
I wouldn't throw this on Director Bu.
He's not ready to go into surgery.

716
00:36:30,396 --> 00:36:33,065
Since when do doctors need to get ready
to save someone from dying?

717
00:36:33,941 --> 00:36:37,612
It's just that it's been such a long
while now since I last operated.

718
00:36:38,237 --> 00:36:39,405
Allow me to assist you, please.

719
00:36:40,323 --> 00:36:42,909
You've completed
over 300 craniotomies to date.

720
00:36:42,992 --> 00:36:48,456
Well, first, I'll need to look at the
materials, we don't have any other option.

721
00:36:48,539 --> 00:36:52,210
You're the only one who can do this
within a 30 minute radius of this place

722
00:36:52,293 --> 00:36:53,586
with the skill this operation will take.

723
00:37:01,385 --> 00:37:04,263
Listen up, people.
This patient is going to be transferred.

724
00:37:05,306 --> 00:37:07,225
Get an ambulance ready
and call Daeseok Hospital now.

725
00:37:07,308 --> 00:37:08,935
We can't do that. There's no time.

726
00:37:09,602 --> 00:37:10,603
The surgery has begun.

727
00:37:19,320 --> 00:37:22,865
We told Dr. Jo Won-jin in anesthesiology,
and she opened an OR to begin.

728
00:37:23,032 --> 00:37:24,617
Who the hell's performing
that surgery, Tae-gyeong?

729
00:37:26,410 --> 00:37:28,037
Dr. Gye Su-jeong is operating.

730
00:37:28,204 --> 00:37:29,205
What? What?

731
00:37:31,874 --> 00:37:36,087
Cranniotomy, an aneurysm neck clipping.
We'll now begin surgery.

732
00:37:37,129 --> 00:37:38,923
Based on the information we pulled,
Director,

733
00:37:39,006 --> 00:37:41,634
Dr. Gye Su-jeong's not
board certified in NS.

734
00:37:41,717 --> 00:37:43,094
Dr. X.

735
00:37:43,219 --> 00:37:46,806
Dr. Do, we absolutely cannot allow this.

736
00:37:48,015 --> 00:37:49,934
We need to stop the surgery
right now, Director.

737
00:38:07,034 --> 00:38:09,036
It's not right. They can't shit.

738
00:38:09,870 --> 00:38:11,414
Vitals are stable, Doctor.

739
00:38:11,497 --> 00:38:12,707
Lidocaine.

740
00:38:39,358 --> 00:38:40,359
Blade.

741
00:38:50,786 --> 00:38:51,787
Dandy clip.

742
00:38:57,752 --> 00:39:00,921
Sorry, I'm only calling
to ask you for a favor.

743
00:39:01,547 --> 00:39:03,799
look, you're gonna have to send
that email out ASAP.

744
00:39:05,634 --> 00:39:10,222
I know I should have something ready.
Well, you know how it is.

745
00:39:10,306 --> 00:39:14,268
Some people just won't buy it, even when
it's right there staring them in the face.

746
00:39:16,103 --> 00:39:17,980
Oh great, I owe you big.

747
00:39:19,815 --> 00:39:21,776
Who gave that woman permission
to perform surgery?

748
00:39:21,859 --> 00:39:23,402
Do you people have no empathy?

749
00:39:23,486 --> 00:39:25,154
Saving sick patients
is what a doctor does.

750
00:39:25,237 --> 00:39:27,907
You're sure she can perform the surgery?
Does she know what she's doing?

751
00:39:30,493 --> 00:39:32,870
Director, is she,
is she doing this correctly?

752
00:39:33,788 --> 00:39:36,916
Yes, and actually
she's executing this perfectly.

753
00:39:37,750 --> 00:39:38,751
Good God.

754
00:39:40,044 --> 00:39:41,462
This is driving me insane.

755
00:39:41,545 --> 00:39:43,214
What the hell? Is she crazy for surgeries?

756
00:39:43,297 --> 00:39:45,091
She doesn't even have
an NS board certification.

757
00:39:46,550 --> 00:39:49,553
Dr. Do, you can't stop the surgery.
The operation has begun.

758
00:39:49,637 --> 00:39:51,138
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

759
00:39:51,222 --> 00:39:53,933
Dr. Gye said before she knows
how to perform this procedure,

760
00:39:54,016 --> 00:39:55,017
she can do this operation.

761
00:39:55,101 --> 00:39:56,102
And how would you know that?

762
00:39:56,143 --> 00:39:57,436
Come on, it's clear as day.

763
00:39:57,520 --> 00:39:59,480
Even I know she can.
So how can none of you?

764
00:39:59,563 --> 00:40:02,400
You've seen her in action already, and now
you're watching her do it right there.

765
00:40:02,483 --> 00:40:03,776
Oh, you little shit, get.

766
00:40:03,859 --> 00:40:06,987
Listen. Whether we transfer her or wait,
it'll be too late for a treatment.

767
00:40:07,071 --> 00:40:10,533
If we face that risk no matter what,
Shouldn't we try our best with a doctor

768
00:40:10,616 --> 00:40:12,326
capable of performing the surgery?

769
00:40:12,410 --> 00:40:14,078
Have you all gone insane?

770
00:40:14,161 --> 00:40:17,123
Do you really think a doctor
who's not NS certified can do this?

771
00:40:19,458 --> 00:40:20,459
Hey, Gye Su--

772
00:40:21,710 --> 00:40:26,715
What th-- hey! Test, test. Hello--
what? What's wrong with this shitty thing.

773
00:40:27,550 --> 00:40:29,093
I'm sorry, doctor.

774
00:40:29,176 --> 00:40:32,388
Hey, I'm sorry, give me that, you little.

775
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:37,184
I'll talk to Dr. Gye myself.

776
00:40:41,480 --> 00:40:43,941
Oh goodness, Director Bu, good morning.

777
00:40:44,984 --> 00:40:49,196
This shows Dr. Gye is NS board
certified as per your standards?

778
00:40:50,865 --> 00:40:51,866
What the--

779
00:40:53,033 --> 00:40:55,119
What? Seriously?

780
00:40:55,202 --> 00:40:57,371
Director, you still can't let her do this.

781
00:40:57,455 --> 00:40:58,914
Periosteal elevator.

782
00:40:58,998 --> 00:41:00,833
- Reconnect that right now!
- I'm sorry, I can't.

783
00:41:00,916 --> 00:41:03,461
- Give it to me! I said give it to me.
- Please, I'm sorry.

784
00:41:03,544 --> 00:41:04,545
Doctor Gye needs to focus!

785
00:41:04,628 --> 00:41:06,964
- Let Doctor Gye work, damn it!
- I'll reconnect it myself!

786
00:41:07,673 --> 00:41:09,341
Let go, you little nerd. Let go!

787
00:41:09,425 --> 00:41:10,593
What the hell do you think you're doing?

788
00:41:10,676 --> 00:41:12,178
- Park Tae-gyeong, you're fired.
- What?

789
00:41:12,261 --> 00:41:13,512
We need to be able to talk to the OR.

790
00:41:18,559 --> 00:41:20,436
We need to stop this surgery, now!

791
00:41:22,188 --> 00:41:25,399
I'll fix it in place. The fissure, please.

792
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:39,788
If we don't succeed,
this patient will die in the place she

793
00:41:39,872 --> 00:41:41,832
worked hard to keep clean every day.

794
00:41:41,916 --> 00:41:44,126
There isn't a single place
in this hospital she hasn't touched,

795
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:46,962
so with that, let's see this through.

796
00:41:47,755 --> 00:41:49,048
Yes, doctor.

797
00:41:49,131 --> 00:41:51,091
I'll now be doing
a burr hole trephination.

798
00:41:53,844 --> 00:41:56,555
I think that Dr. Su-jeong
already knew in advance.

799
00:41:57,223 --> 00:41:58,641
She knew the patient would collapse. Huh?

800
00:41:58,724 --> 00:42:00,142
What are you saying?

801
00:42:00,226 --> 00:42:02,102
She'd been sleeping
in that ER bed since dawn.

802
00:42:03,103 --> 00:42:05,481
I think she was waiting for that patient.

803
00:42:07,441 --> 00:42:10,069
Director,
I don't buy that board certification.

804
00:42:10,152 --> 00:42:11,028
Let's just go down there.

805
00:42:12,655 --> 00:42:16,116
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong, your actions are
gonna massively haunt your career.

806
00:42:16,200 --> 00:42:17,868
Is that understood?

807
00:42:17,952 --> 00:42:22,164
Yes, I was thinking that at first too,
but after seeing the monitor.

808
00:42:22,957 --> 00:42:25,000
I understand what they meant now.

809
00:42:25,084 --> 00:42:27,461
Who is this woman exactly
and why did she come here?

810
00:43:11,630 --> 00:43:12,631
Clip.

811
00:43:14,550 --> 00:43:17,761
- She found the neck that quick, my God.
- That speed.

812
00:43:21,223 --> 00:43:22,600
Clipping now.

813
00:43:39,408 --> 00:43:41,910
The clipping is successful, doctor.

814
00:43:44,913 --> 00:43:46,081
Bipolar.

815
00:43:49,793 --> 00:43:52,338
Doctor! Dr. Gye Su-jeong!

816
00:43:53,255 --> 00:43:56,342
Doctor.

817
00:43:58,469 --> 00:43:59,845
Is this on?

818
00:44:03,432 --> 00:44:07,144
Hey Dr. Gye, they're making galbijjim
in the cafeteria for lunch today.

819
00:44:07,227 --> 00:44:09,688
I'll save a seat for you, Doctor.
You did an incredible job.

820
00:44:28,957 --> 00:44:31,835
- Good job, everyone.
- Good job good job, everyone.

821
00:45:23,804 --> 00:45:26,890
Could the aneurysm re-rupture
or cause another issue?

822
00:45:26,974 --> 00:45:29,977
The surgery was performed beautifully.

823
00:45:30,728 --> 00:45:32,855
It's truly been years
since I've seen work like this.

824
00:45:32,938 --> 00:45:36,567
Then I suppose as it relates to the
hospital, I would say this is good news.

825
00:45:36,650 --> 00:45:37,735
Yes.

826
00:45:38,944 --> 00:45:40,946
I certainly will agree with that.

827
00:45:43,490 --> 00:45:45,451
Let's head outside and have a talk.

828
00:46:01,341 --> 00:46:02,676
SUGAR SYRUP

829
00:46:37,252 --> 00:46:39,379
I had a KMA meeting.

830
00:46:39,463 --> 00:46:41,215
You should have rushed here
from your conference.

831
00:46:41,298 --> 00:46:43,842
- You were sightseeing.
- I took the day off to rest.

832
00:46:43,926 --> 00:46:44,968
Is that a crime?

833
00:46:45,052 --> 00:46:46,845
You're the one who rushed
to the KMA on a whim.

834
00:46:46,929 --> 00:46:49,681
It was an emergency.
Should I have skipped a meeting?

835
00:46:49,765 --> 00:46:51,558
They're trying to destroy us right now.

836
00:46:51,642 --> 00:46:55,229
- I had to be at that meeting.
- Gentlemen, I'd rather you quiet down.

837
00:46:55,312 --> 00:46:56,855
Is this really
why you asked for this meeting?

838
00:46:59,399 --> 00:47:00,901
Dr. Jo.

839
00:47:00,984 --> 00:47:04,613
I never would have guessed
you'd open an OR to anyone, huh?

840
00:47:04,696 --> 00:47:07,741
Is this reverse discrimination
because she's a woman?

841
00:47:07,825 --> 00:47:09,576
I wouldn't have opened
that OR for you if you were a woman,

842
00:47:09,660 --> 00:47:11,036
she would have died.

843
00:47:11,119 --> 00:47:12,955
- What's that?
- Dr. Jo.

844
00:47:13,038 --> 00:47:15,874
No matter how pressing that surgery was,
we were in the middle of a conference,

845
00:47:15,958 --> 00:47:17,876
What's the point of being at a conference
if patients die

846
00:47:17,960 --> 00:47:19,711
'cause we're not here to operate?

847
00:47:19,795 --> 00:47:23,048
Wow, I can see the discipline
around here has really gone to hell.

848
00:47:23,131 --> 00:47:26,718
We are not your equals.
Some of us have decades more experience.

849
00:47:26,802 --> 00:47:29,263
Director, what happened
was completely unacceptable.

850
00:47:29,346 --> 00:47:30,889
- They should have waited.
- No, if we'd waited,

851
00:47:30,973 --> 00:47:32,516
the patient would have died.

852
00:47:33,225 --> 00:47:34,434
What?

853
00:47:34,518 --> 00:47:37,771
You all should thank God she was at
a hospital, that she remained conscious,

854
00:47:37,855 --> 00:47:41,024
and that there was an excellent doctor
here who was ready to go to work.

855
00:47:41,108 --> 00:47:43,068
Had she gotten here a year earlier,
then maybe EMTs.

856
00:47:43,151 --> 00:47:44,653
Sir.

857
00:47:44,736 --> 00:47:47,281
Don't play that card.
We've already gone through that.

858
00:47:47,364 --> 00:47:49,074
It was you who posted it.

859
00:47:49,157 --> 00:47:51,159
It was you who leaked
the video to the press.

860
00:47:52,661 --> 00:47:55,289
It makes sense when I look at it now.

861
00:47:55,372 --> 00:47:59,001
You spent years together in the ER,
and by that point you were close comrades.

862
00:47:59,751 --> 00:48:02,254
Deliberately, we let the doctors
out of our investigation.

863
00:48:02,337 --> 00:48:04,548
EMTs and nurses know
there are bigger issues.

864
00:48:04,631 --> 00:48:09,595
They could have leaked, and so we had
to be positive they wouldn't be heard.

865
00:48:14,099 --> 00:48:17,936
- You're right, I was the whistleblower.
- Dr. Kim.

866
00:48:18,020 --> 00:48:20,147
I didn't take you for a backstabber.

867
00:48:20,230 --> 00:48:22,399
Do you see the hell
that I've been through?

868
00:48:22,482 --> 00:48:24,610
- Everyone around me was going crazy.
- Director.

869
00:48:24,693 --> 00:48:27,571
You must report Dr. Kim
to the ethics Committee for censure.

870
00:48:27,654 --> 00:48:30,949
Our entire lives were completely
upended by him and his reckless stunt.

871
00:48:31,033 --> 00:48:32,534
Perhaps you should explain.

872
00:48:33,660 --> 00:48:35,245
EMT saw.

873
00:48:36,496 --> 00:48:38,332
He had a one year old daughter
he left behind,

874
00:48:38,415 --> 00:48:41,251
and now with him gone,
that poor girl doesn't have a dad.

875
00:48:41,960 --> 00:48:45,047
Yes, I leaked it to the press.
I couldn't believe what I'd heard.

876
00:48:45,130 --> 00:48:47,925
Doctors ducking accountability and putting
his death on him,

877
00:48:48,008 --> 00:48:51,094
saying that it was just bad luck
or that it was his fate,

878
00:48:51,178 --> 00:48:53,305
or he'd be dead whether or not they tried.
So who cares?

879
00:48:53,388 --> 00:48:55,974
That made my blood run cold.
That's why I chose to upload it.

880
00:48:56,058 --> 00:48:58,143
How dare you talk to Director Bu
with such insubordinance?

881
00:48:58,226 --> 00:48:59,603
I had to upload it cause you
weren't listening,

882
00:48:59,686 --> 00:49:01,188
which is exactly
what you're doing right now.

883
00:49:01,271 --> 00:49:02,689
because everyone knows coil embolization

884
00:49:02,773 --> 00:49:05,484
won't work when intracranial pressure
is as high as it was.

885
00:49:05,567 --> 00:49:08,654
Even if we performed a craniotomy
on the patient right then and there,

886
00:49:08,737 --> 00:49:10,030
it would've been too late.

887
00:49:10,113 --> 00:49:11,949
You're really saying
the hospital did everything right

888
00:49:12,032 --> 00:49:13,241
and bears no responsibility?

889
00:49:14,368 --> 00:49:16,954
There is no way I will sit here
and pretend that's true.

890
00:49:17,037 --> 00:49:18,330
If we just chalk it up to EMT cell's fate,

891
00:49:18,413 --> 00:49:20,248
nothing will change
and nothing will be learned.

892
00:49:20,332 --> 00:49:22,459
Dr. Kim, are you accusing us
of malpractice?

893
00:49:22,542 --> 00:49:25,170
Are you saying that we bear accountability
for this tragedy?

894
00:49:25,253 --> 00:49:28,465
Are you with your patients
24 hours a day, every day of the year?

895
00:49:28,548 --> 00:49:30,842
It would appear
that's what you're expecting.

896
00:49:30,926 --> 00:49:32,302
Doctors are human too.

897
00:49:37,849 --> 00:49:39,351
Oh.

898
00:49:42,187 --> 00:49:44,648
- Who called Dr. Gye?
- I'm sleepy.

899
00:49:45,732 --> 00:49:49,111
- Hey, Dr. Gye, we'll deal with you later.
- You should go.

900
00:49:51,488 --> 00:49:55,659
Are you fellows the only humans?
Your patients are also human.

901
00:49:57,411 --> 00:50:00,205
Fella? Did she just call me--

902
00:50:00,288 --> 00:50:02,666
Young lady,
you will refer to me as "Doctor".

903
00:50:06,920 --> 00:50:12,676
Okay, so then you're a doctor
who has no real desire to be a doctor?

904
00:50:13,427 --> 00:50:15,762
You're just like any other person
with any other job.

905
00:50:15,846 --> 00:50:19,016
At what point exactly
does your work as a doctor begin?

906
00:50:19,850 --> 00:50:23,937
Ah, only when you're on the clock,
when you're here at the hospital,

907
00:50:24,021 --> 00:50:26,189
mornings, nights.

908
00:50:26,273 --> 00:50:28,567
How dare you, stupid girl.

909
00:50:29,067 --> 00:50:31,862
- You'll be gone in no time.
- Let's watch our language, people.

910
00:50:31,945 --> 00:50:35,157
Dr. Gye, apologize to
these doctors right now!

911
00:50:35,240 --> 00:50:37,034
Yeo Jeong-soon needs us.

912
00:50:37,576 --> 00:50:40,662
She doesn't usually work today,
but she still chose to work.

913
00:50:41,246 --> 00:50:43,915
She was helping another employee
on the cleaning crew

914
00:50:43,999 --> 00:50:46,752
who unexpectedly went
home to deal with a sudden emergency.

915
00:50:48,295 --> 00:50:52,549
She's someone who takes out your trash
while you're home with your families.

916
00:50:52,632 --> 00:50:55,052
Well, it sounds like it was a good thing
she chose to work.

917
00:50:55,135 --> 00:50:56,470
Imagine if she stayed home, huh?

918
00:50:56,553 --> 00:50:58,597
Sounds like she got lucky.

919
00:50:58,680 --> 00:51:02,350
I just can't believe the words I'm
hearing from you about a person, you know.

920
00:51:02,434 --> 00:51:04,019
How about you show just a little concern?

921
00:51:04,102 --> 00:51:06,229
She's lucky she collapsed here
where she can get care.

922
00:51:06,313 --> 00:51:09,524
Wow, that's, so that's the reason
there's still garbage in the can.

923
00:51:09,608 --> 00:51:11,818
She should have at least
asked someone to cover for her.

924
00:51:11,902 --> 00:51:13,904
How irresponsible, Dr. Tom.

925
00:51:13,987 --> 00:51:15,072
What?

926
00:51:16,948 --> 00:51:18,075
What do you think you're doing?

927
00:51:18,158 --> 00:51:20,619
Dr. Gye, are you gonna
keep behaving this way?

928
00:51:20,702 --> 00:51:23,038
- We don't act like that.
- Hey.

929
00:51:23,121 --> 00:51:24,873
You really think you're above the rules?

930
00:51:24,956 --> 00:51:27,542
Medicine is a smaller community
than you think.

931
00:51:27,626 --> 00:51:30,253
You'll be blacklisted
from every hospital in Korea.

932
00:51:30,337 --> 00:51:32,506
Why did you hire this wretch, Ms. Lee?

933
00:51:32,589 --> 00:51:35,217
Mark my words, that operation
was completed incorrectly.

934
00:51:35,300 --> 00:51:37,385
When that rupture happens,
it'll be on your watch.

935
00:51:37,469 --> 00:51:39,596
If not, then I'll hand
my white coat to you, huh?

936
00:51:39,679 --> 00:51:40,889
Yeah, sure, I'll throw mine in too.

937
00:51:40,972 --> 00:51:43,433
Let's hope he's wrong,
and I know he's not. You better be sure.

938
00:51:43,517 --> 00:51:45,018
You're sure she performed
the operation correctly?

939
00:51:45,102 --> 00:51:47,395
Are you willing to risk
a patient's life on it?

940
00:51:48,647 --> 00:51:51,525
Are you sure?
What about a rupture of the aneurysm?

941
00:51:51,608 --> 00:51:53,193
- Are you prepared for complications?
- Dr. Jo,

942
00:51:53,276 --> 00:51:55,278
if we don't open an operating room,
another person will die.

943
00:51:55,362 --> 00:51:58,824
I couldn't possibly open up an OR for
someone who isn't board certified in NS.

944
00:51:58,907 --> 00:52:00,117
But I can be.

945
00:52:00,867 --> 00:52:02,035
What'd you say?

946
00:52:02,702 --> 00:52:06,873
I think you know, I know I can do this.
Dr. Jo, please, we're running out of time.

947
00:52:06,957 --> 00:52:08,375
I'm reporting this to Director Bu.

948
00:52:09,126 --> 00:52:10,669
You said it yourself, Dr. Jo.

949
00:52:10,752 --> 00:52:13,713
In this situation, you would hope
that one of those 130 brain surgeons

950
00:52:13,797 --> 00:52:14,923
is at the hospital that day.

951
00:52:15,632 --> 00:52:19,970
Dr. Jo, one of those 130 doctors
is right here standing in front of us.

952
00:52:20,053 --> 00:52:22,931
Please, Dr. Jo, come on, we're
talking about our hospital's custodian.

953
00:52:23,014 --> 00:52:24,432
Everyone will miss her.

954
00:52:24,516 --> 00:52:27,060
I bet she even cleaned the phone
you're holding this morning.

955
00:52:31,064 --> 00:52:34,401
Park Tae-gyeong. Listen closely.

956
00:52:34,484 --> 00:52:37,070
What's most important is that one
doctor must have properly trained

957
00:52:37,154 --> 00:52:38,905
for the surgery
they're going to undertake.

958
00:52:38,989 --> 00:52:40,448
Does this doctor understand it in theory,

959
00:52:40,532 --> 00:52:42,868
or are they truly ready to handle
an operation that's life or death?

960
00:52:47,372 --> 00:52:48,373
Min-gu,

961
00:52:49,791 --> 00:52:52,085
you threatening my career
doesn't scare me at all.

962
00:52:56,840 --> 00:52:58,175
Polish your resumes.

963
00:52:59,009 --> 00:53:01,219
Wait a second.
Where the hell do you think you're going?

964
00:53:02,262 --> 00:53:04,389
Bitching at me for staying,
bitching at me for leaving.

965
00:53:04,472 --> 00:53:05,765
What does this dude want?

966
00:53:06,474 --> 00:53:07,559
Bitching?

967
00:53:08,977 --> 00:53:10,562
This girl's gone completely mental.

968
00:53:10,645 --> 00:53:13,648
Director.
We need to fire her right now, okay?

969
00:53:13,732 --> 00:53:15,734
Her actions could bring
down the entire hospital.

970
00:53:15,817 --> 00:53:18,486
We need to make sure
she doesn't work in medicine ever again.

971
00:53:18,570 --> 00:53:19,571
Stop.

972
00:53:23,200 --> 00:53:24,993
Aren't you ashamed?

973
00:53:25,493 --> 00:53:26,953
You love taking credit for simple cases,

974
00:53:27,037 --> 00:53:29,998
but when you get a patient who's about to
die, you jump and running for the hills.

975
00:53:31,625 --> 00:53:36,504
Unfettered cowardice. Spineless fools.

976
00:53:46,723 --> 00:53:49,309
- You still haven't gone in?
- No, no.

977
00:53:49,392 --> 00:53:51,144
Their conversation's
taking a while, I guess.

978
00:53:58,193 --> 00:53:59,444
Sorry about earlier.

979
00:54:00,612 --> 00:54:02,489
- Which thing earlier?
- Which thing?

980
00:54:03,365 --> 00:54:04,574
Am I really that mean to you?

981
00:54:04,658 --> 00:54:07,786
- Oh, earlier in the observation gallery.
- No, not that.

982
00:54:07,869 --> 00:54:09,287
I was gonna say sorry about when I
got angry

983
00:54:09,371 --> 00:54:12,999
and I poked you in the chest outside
the OR when we were talking earlier

984
00:54:13,083 --> 00:54:15,418
- Oh, that thing.
- You know...

985
00:54:16,294 --> 00:54:18,421
you got a knack
for getting people really mad.

986
00:54:18,505 --> 00:54:19,714
And I was also in the wrong.

987
00:54:20,298 --> 00:54:22,550
I was being rude, so I'm really sorry.

988
00:54:22,634 --> 00:54:25,971
I just got ahead of myself
and I couldn't accept the fact

989
00:54:26,054 --> 00:54:29,140
that the institution I chose could let
something so horrible slide like that.

990
00:54:29,224 --> 00:54:30,517
Just forget all that.

991
00:54:30,600 --> 00:54:36,398
I, um, Honestly,
I won't say I don't understand.

992
00:54:41,653 --> 00:54:44,155
Uh, but as an intern I'd just
quietly finish a month with us

993
00:54:44,239 --> 00:54:45,115
and then go on your way.

994
00:54:45,198 --> 00:54:48,118
I really don't want to see any more
interns doing a rotation in surgery,

995
00:54:48,201 --> 00:54:49,828
pretending to be doctors
with some great sense of duty

996
00:54:49,911 --> 00:54:52,998
only to go to an
easier department somewhere.

997
00:54:54,958 --> 00:54:56,876
You won't be a surgeon anyway.

998
00:55:02,465 --> 00:55:04,259
Oh, there you are. Why are you alone?

999
00:55:04,342 --> 00:55:05,343
Where's the--

1000
00:55:06,177 --> 00:55:10,223
- Why are you by yourself?
- Then, what… What the hell am I gonna do?

1001
00:55:11,891 --> 00:55:17,022
What kind of doctor should I be?
Can I actually be a doctor?

1002
00:55:17,731 --> 00:55:19,607
Tell Park Tae-gyeong or
whatever to come in right now!

1003
00:55:19,691 --> 00:55:22,944
This is all because of that damn intern
in the observation gallery.

1004
00:55:23,028 --> 00:55:26,364
I guess there's no point in worrying.
I won't live to see it.

1005
00:56:16,373 --> 00:56:18,375
I would like to thank you all
for coming today.

1006
00:56:18,458 --> 00:56:19,542
It's much appreciated.

1007
00:56:20,377 --> 00:56:24,381
I am the new director to be serving
you all here at the GUMC,

1008
00:56:24,464 --> 00:56:26,091
Mister Bu Seung-gwon.

1009
00:56:26,174 --> 00:56:29,803
In lieu of traditional ceremony,
I decided to hold this press conference

1010
00:56:29,886 --> 00:56:33,848
because today marks one year
of the death of EMT So.,

1011
00:56:33,932 --> 00:56:37,310
who tragically died on duty
in our ER last year.

1012
00:56:37,394 --> 00:56:39,646
Although that tragic event happened a
while ago,

1013
00:56:39,729 --> 00:56:42,857
it recently came up that there
was another similar case at our hospital.

1014
00:56:43,691 --> 00:56:46,820
A contractor collapsed recently
from a brain aneurysm.

1015
00:56:47,487 --> 00:56:49,447
While she was on duty
here at our hospital.

1016
00:56:49,948 --> 00:56:54,619
In response, our medical staff did
their best to provide her with treatment.

1017
00:56:55,537 --> 00:56:56,704
I would like to propose

1018
00:56:58,123 --> 00:57:02,085
an opportunity to say what our
earlier director chose not to bring up.

1019
00:57:02,877 --> 00:57:05,422
The death of EMT Seo Jin-yeong

1020
00:57:05,505 --> 00:57:08,716
was an event that revealed problems
in our medical community.

1021
00:57:08,800 --> 00:57:11,261
Medical fees that are running us dry.

1022
00:57:11,928 --> 00:57:15,265
A chronic lack of personnel,
budget shortfalls.

1023
00:57:15,348 --> 00:57:16,599
Yes, you heard me right.

1024
00:57:16,683 --> 00:57:21,521
All these things are true, however,
those issues aren't the whole story.

1025
00:57:22,272 --> 00:57:27,360
Firstly, here we must uphold a certain
trust in each other and our system,

1026
00:57:27,444 --> 00:57:31,156
the belief that as long
as you're working at this hospital,

1027
00:57:31,239 --> 00:57:33,575
should you ever be injured or fall down,

1028
00:57:33,658 --> 00:57:36,244
that you will promptly receive
appropriate medical treatment

1029
00:57:36,327 --> 00:57:37,579
regardless of your title.

1030
00:57:38,204 --> 00:57:40,999
And after being treated, go back home.

1031
00:57:41,082 --> 00:57:46,504
This hospital
has failed to uphold that vow.

1032
00:57:47,589 --> 00:57:50,133
As a result of that,
for the very first time,

1033
00:57:50,216 --> 00:57:53,928
I would like to
offer a sincere apology to Seo's family,

1034
00:57:54,012 --> 00:57:57,724
the people of this country
who we've clearly greatly disappointed.

1035
00:57:58,641 --> 00:58:00,018
And our team here

1036
00:58:15,742 --> 00:58:17,160
I will now take your questions.

1037
00:58:21,498 --> 00:58:22,624
How interesting.

1038
00:58:22,707 --> 00:58:25,502
How interesting. The video… Kim
Seong-jin didn't leak it online.

1039
00:58:28,296 --> 00:58:29,589
It was you who did it.

1040
00:58:31,049 --> 00:58:33,760
I guess his guilt got to him
where he thought he'd killed him.

1041
00:58:33,843 --> 00:58:36,221
I just thought
it was the right thing to do.

1042
00:58:36,304 --> 00:58:38,848
You were relentless.
You kept asking me to send you that video.

1043
00:58:38,932 --> 00:58:40,975
You swore things would change
when you leaked the truth.

1044
00:58:41,059 --> 00:58:42,519
Begged that I trust you.

1045
00:58:42,602 --> 00:58:44,229
Well, do you feel
like things are changing?

1046
00:58:53,738 --> 00:58:55,448
Ah Let's see how this progresses.

1047
00:58:56,157 --> 00:58:57,158
This is just the start.

1048
00:59:06,668 --> 00:59:10,213
<i>The newly appointed director's actions</i>
<i>regarding the tragic death of EMT </i>

1049
00:59:10,296 --> 00:59:13,758
<i>Seo Jin-yeong at Guseo University</i>
<i>Medical Center are unusual.</i>

1050
00:59:14,467 --> 00:59:16,803
<i>Director Wu Hong Guan bowed his head in</i>
<i>apology </i>

1051
00:59:16,886 --> 00:59:19,055
<i>for the mistakes of the previous</i>
<i>director, </i>

1052
00:59:19,138 --> 00:59:22,058
<i>stating that he would cooperate</i>
<i>with the bereaved family's appeal.</i>

1053
00:59:23,434 --> 00:59:26,729
<i>He also expressed his desire to</i>
<i>meet with Seo Jin-yeong's family.</i>

1054
00:59:28,189 --> 00:59:31,484
<i>According to hospital officials,</i>
<i>Director Bu chose to make this statement</i>

1055
00:59:31,568 --> 00:59:34,946
<i>in lieu of a ceremony commemorating</i>
<i>the start of his directorship.</i>

1056
00:59:36,197 --> 00:59:39,117
All right, so this is the new contract
you've come up with.

1057
00:59:39,200 --> 00:59:41,744
Yes, by now, surely you're aware,

1058
00:59:41,828 --> 00:59:44,706
Dr. Gye Su-jeong is a highly
exceptional surgeon

1059
00:59:44,789 --> 00:59:47,417
as well as a talented
neurovascular specialist,

1060
00:59:48,042 --> 00:59:51,671
and she's recently filled a gap in care
at Guoo University Medical Center.

1061
00:59:51,754 --> 00:59:54,716
Ah, I've already sent you
a separate invoice for that.

1062
00:59:54,799 --> 00:59:56,801
Oh, so you're trying to get
a little extra money.

1063
00:59:56,884 --> 00:59:58,595
Now with this case,

1064
00:59:58,678 --> 01:00:01,180
didn't she already
prove she's worth the extra money?

1065
01:00:02,265 --> 01:00:05,226
- Then are the other terms the same?
- Actually, we have another one.

1066
01:00:05,310 --> 01:00:07,437
- What would that entail?
- I will not work in any wing

1067
01:00:07,520 --> 01:00:10,815
- that I do not want to be in.
- How dare you? You work on contract.

1068
01:00:10,898 --> 01:00:12,442
You work wherever we need you.

1069
01:00:24,287 --> 01:00:27,165
You've hit some roadblocks while
dealing with the current administration.

1070
01:00:27,248 --> 01:00:29,751
There have been rumblings
of another health workers' strike soon.

1071
01:00:29,834 --> 01:00:34,213
If a gap in medical services occurs
or if a major accident were to happen...

1072
01:00:34,297 --> 01:00:37,550
Oh no, my heart just breaks
over the thought.

1073
01:00:37,634 --> 01:00:40,511
Then I wonder who would
be ready to fill that gap.

1074
01:00:40,595 --> 01:00:42,305
So, Dr. Gye Su-jeong
will rescue the hospital

1075
01:00:42,388 --> 01:00:45,725
Uh, no, not quite.
Your money will rescue you.

1076
01:00:45,808 --> 01:00:48,770
No matter how precarious
this hospital situation is,

1077
01:00:48,853 --> 01:00:52,315
it's still a branch of a foundation
that profits billions of won a year.

1078
01:00:52,398 --> 01:00:54,901
You could loosen the purse
strings a little, am I right?

1079
01:00:57,362 --> 01:00:59,906
Now let me look over the rate
and the terms again.

1080
01:00:59,989 --> 01:01:03,159
So first, the terms of employment
in regards to working

1081
01:01:03,242 --> 01:01:05,119
- outside of work hours--
- Just a moment.

1082
01:01:10,500 --> 01:01:12,126
We're ready. You can go ahead.

1083
01:01:13,586 --> 01:01:14,921
He's ready to come in.

1084
01:01:15,004 --> 01:01:18,007
Gentlemen, what is going on
at this critical juncture?

1085
01:01:28,393 --> 01:01:31,270
- It's been a while, Director.
- How have you been?

1086
01:01:31,354 --> 01:01:34,148
You look quite well. Take a seat.

1087
01:01:39,362 --> 01:01:41,739
Ah, why don't you two
introduce yourselves?

1088
01:01:41,823 --> 01:01:43,616
- This is...
- My name's Na Dae-il

1089
01:01:44,117 --> 01:01:46,369
I'll be joining the hospital
as a general surgeon as of today.

1090
01:01:47,120 --> 01:01:48,287
Pleasure to meet you.

1091
01:01:55,920 --> 01:01:58,005
The contract is on hold for now.

1092
01:03:11,120 --> 01:03:12,914
So thoughts on Dr. Na.
He's good, isn't he?

1093
01:03:12,997 --> 01:03:14,582
Straighten your
shoulders. You're Gye Su-jeong.

1094
01:03:15,124 --> 01:03:17,418
- Call the OR.
- Why would you march into

1095
01:03:17,502 --> 01:03:19,170
someone else's OR and cause trouble?

1096
01:03:19,253 --> 01:03:20,713
I heard something happened
with Dr. Na Dae-il.

1097
01:03:20,797 --> 01:03:22,965
That bastard's hands stink.

1098
01:03:23,049 --> 01:03:25,343
Okay, so what are you gonna do
about the surgery?

1099
01:03:25,426 --> 01:03:27,512
Wow, relationships are
scary sometimes, huh?

1100
01:03:27,595 --> 01:03:30,932
I gotta say, I'm rather curious
to know exactly what lies ahead.

1101
01:03:31,015 --> 01:03:32,099
Only looking ahead.

1102
01:03:33,643 --> 01:03:36,521
She seemed like a god or a monster.
